	"comments": [
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " The TERMINAL `=>`→body gap of a curried arrow chain is answered by the same emitters",
			"start": 20,
			"end": 107
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " the default arrow layout's `=>`→body arms use, so a run the author BROKE AFTER keeps",
			"start": 109,
			"end": 196
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " its break wherever that machinery keeps it — across every body kind, and whether the",
			"start": 198,
			"end": 285
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " break is forced by a multi-line block in the run or by the body's own hard break.",
			"start": 287,
			"end": 371
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " a body whose own doc breaks forces the run's break: a multi-line template",
